Shared drifted-anchor extraction contract in which git span history's current section builds each live snapshot from a single normalized read of the anchored location — the resolver's own worktree conversion, so the rendered body and the rk64 token beside it are always the same bytes and a content filter can never make one object describe two files — read at the resolver's healed location for the bytes-equal relocation statuses drift prints 'moved to' for and back at the declared address for every other status, with existence asked before content so a missing file is never conflated with an empty one, and applies the commit path's policy on all three axes: strict-decoding the bytes so a non-UTF-8 live side classifies as structurally unavailable exactly like the commit path, slicing the declared range through git.rs's single slice_line_range so a range with no overlap past end-of-file classifies as range-past-eof instead of fabricating an empty text side, and failing closed on a filter that produces no content so the resolver's FilterFailed reason reaches the output as filter-failed rather than collapsing into absent, with the resolver's nothing-resolves arm re-asking the declared address so 'nothing resolved' and 'no such file' stay different facts.
